    {
      "id": "36cf165a-6a8d-4508-927b-8fbf2503f97c",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        464,
        -144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#FEEA87",
        "width": 560,
        "height": 1128,
        "content": "## 📍 Zip Code in Radius + Market Summary — Searchbug (api_zipradius)\n\nFind every ZIP code within a given distance of a center ZIP — with city, state, population and business counts — then turn that list into a ranked coverage table AND a one-row market summary per search. Works for a single ZIP or a whole CSV of ZIPs.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Single:** enter a center ZIP + distance in miles. **Bulk:** leave ZIP blank and upload a CSV (zip, distance, min_population).\n2. Normalize Input accepts either path, pads short ZIPs back to 5 digits (2138 → 02138) and defaults a missing distance to 5 miles.\n3. Validate Input routes rows with a 5-digit ZIP and a 1–100 mile radius to the API; bad rows are logged as INVALID_INPUT instead of failing the run.\n4. Flatten & Rank ZIPs expands the response into one row per ZIP, sorts by distance, and adds rank, radius band, businesses per 1k people and employees per business. Min Population filters out small ZIPs.\n5. Two sheets are written:\n   • **Zip Code in Radius** — one row per ZIP in the radius\n   • **Zip Radius Summary** — one row per search: ZIP/city counts, totals, largest + nearest city, and a HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW market tier.\n\n### How to set up\n- [ ] Add your Searchbug CO_CODE + PASS in the HTTP Request (Body Parameters)\n- [ ] Connect your OWN Google Sheets account in BOTH Save nodes\n- [ ] Point them at your own spreadsheet and create two tabs:\n      • \"Zip Code in Radius\" (15 columns — see Save ZIP Detail)\n      • \"Zip Radius Summary\" (15 columns — see Save Market Summary)\n- [ ] Activate and share the form link\n\n### Use it for\nTerritory planning, store or service-area coverage, local ad targeting, franchise site selection, and shipping-zone lists.\n\n### Customization\n- Start small (5–10 mi) for cities, larger (25–50 mi) for rural areas.\n- Set Min Population to skip rural ZIPs with almost no businesses.\n- Change the market tier thresholds in Radius Market Summary.\n- Add a Slack or email alert after Save Market Summary."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "90e5ca69-3eb9-4910-81ae-fabdddbb23c6",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1088,
        -144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 596,
        "height": 848,
        "content": "## 1. Single or Bulk Input\n\nSingle or Bulk? checks whether the Zip field was filled. Single → straight to Normalize Input; CSV upload → Extract CSV first.\n\nNormalize Input standardizes the column names (zip / ZIP / zip_code / postal_code, distance / radius / miles) so both paths share one schema."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5b0a9563-f7bc-4181-bd8f-e148794edb61",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1712,
        -144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 620,
        "height": 848,
        "content": "## 2. Clean & Validate\n\nSet Search Input strips non-digits from the ZIP, restores leading zeros (2138 → 02138) and defaults a missing distance to 5 miles.\n\nValidate Input then sends only rows with a real 5-digit ZIP and a 1–100 mile radius to the API. Everything else is logged as INVALID_INPUT so one bad CSV row never kills the run."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "edd62485-4d6d-408f-876e-d74010d3a6c3",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2352,
        -144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 832,
        "height": 848,
        "content": "## 3. Search & Enrich\n\nThe API node retries up to 3× and keeps going on error, so bulk runs finish. Check Results routes empty or failed responses to No Results.\n\nAttach Search Context carries the center ZIP and radius past the API call. Flatten & Rank ZIPs then makes one row per ZIP, sorted nearest-first, and adds rank, radius band (0-5 / 5-10 / 10-25 / 25-50 / 50+ mi), businesses per 1k people and employees per business — plus the Min Population filter."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "dd3121dc-04d5-4bd7-988b-52e05bcc2ab5",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3200,
        -144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#FCD9DD",
        "width": 704,
        "height": 848,
        "content": "## ⚠️ 4. Save Detail + Market Summary\n\nSave ZIP Detail appends one row per ZIP (15 columns) to the \"Zip Code in Radius\" tab.\n\nRadius Market Summary rolls those ZIPs up into one row per search — ZIP and city counts, states covered, total population / businesses / employees, average and max distance, largest and nearest city, businesses per 1k people, and a HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW market_tier — saved to the \"Zip Radius Summary\" tab.\n\nConnect your OWN Google Sheets credential in both Save nodes and create both tabs with matching row-1 headers.\n\nDon't click ⋮ → Refresh — it erases the column mapping."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
